{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured snapshot-backed XFS storage at /srv/data, proved rollback from deliberate modifications to the exact earlier content, retained a known_good snapshot, and verified persistence through a node restart. RHEL 9.8 and kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8.x86_64 remain unchanged.","actions_performed":["Installed the RHEL-supported LVM2 package without upgrading the OS or kernel.","Created a persistent LVM thin pool and XFS logical volume mounted at /srv/data.","Captured application data in the pre_change snapshot.","Deliberately modified files, permissions, and a symlink, and added/deleted files.","Merged pre_change into the origin and verified an exact manifest match.","Created and retained the known_good snapshot.","Restarted node1 and verified the changed boot identity, active storage service, mounted filesystem, snapshot availability, and intact data."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Snapshot-backed application storage under /srv/data","command_ids":["cmd-ed05a839346d4d5a","cmd-fb62e495cc584b8b","cmd-1db711eb0da94642"],"summary":"/srv/data is an XFS logical volume; pre_change was created from data, and known_good remains as a retained thin snapshot."},{"requirement":"Modify the directory and restore the exact earlier snapshot content","command_ids":["cmd-3a814feacbc246b8","cmd-4f75117214734778","cmd-fcad8da1484048d7"],"summary":"The baseline manifest hash was 7dc5b9c885a92778aaaca391a2ed5e94fa1276b7cb013a570a4bf75def376e7c. Mutation produced a different hash; snapshot merge restored the original hash and cmp confirmed an exact match."},{"requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel","command_ids":["cmd-11eaf9f98fcc440e","cmd-fe02167f851c4650"],"summary":"Before and after the work, node1 reports RHEL 9.8 and kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8.x86_64."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-a4af1a85cbd94b84","cmd-3e9b4fa04ff64671","cmd-29676dda46244b0e","cmd-fe02167f851c4650"],"summary":"Captured healthy baseline with boot ID 3aee314b-4dfc-4c3a-90f6-2b07c621eaa0, received restart acknowledgement, observed new boot ID 8aed7d32-1b4f-478f-8ee3-dafe290d18c3, and proved full recovery: system running, storage service active, /srv/data mounted, known_good present, and data exactly matching the baseline manifest."}]}
